Notebook[{Cell["TransformGroupRepresentations", "ObjectName"], 
  Cell["TransformGroupRepresentations[g] transforms the computed irreps of g \
to a unitary (or unitary T-diagonal) basis, committing all selected irreps \
together.\nTransformGroupRepresentations[g, ids] transforms the irreps with \
the given IDs.", "Usage"], Cell["Status: Alpha.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["TransformGroupRepresentations[g] transforms every computed irrep of g \
whose active representation is not unitary to a unitary basis; \
TransformGroupRepresentations[g, ids] restricts the transform to the given \
irrep IDs.", "Notes"], Cell["Each result is derived from a stored variant and \
verified; a result with the same matrices as a stored variant reuses that \
variant. The selected irreps change together: if any one fails, no active \
variant changes (AtomicTransformFailed). Computing missing irreps with \
ComputeGroupRepresentations instead accepts verified irreps one at a time.", 
   "Notes"], Cell["Basis -> \"UnitaryTDiagonal\" (with a modular assignment) \
re-derives every selected irrep with a diagonal T, ordered by TPhaseOrder and \
normalized by PhaseConvention. By default GAP unitarizes (BSGSAverage, then \
GroupAverage) and diagonalizes, and verifies the result. UnitarizationMethod \
-> \"GeneratorEquations\" with Basis -> \"Unitary\" unitarizes in Wolfram and \
sends the conjugator and scales to GAP, which recomputes and verifies them.", 
   "Notes"], Cell["The work runs in Wolfram instead \[LongDash] \
UnitarizeRepresentation and DiagonalizeRepresentationT on each active \
variant, verified in Wolfram and stored with Tier \"Wolfram\" (exact) or \
\"Numerical\", derived from the active variant, with the methods used as its \
source method \[LongDash] for Arithmetic -> \"Numerical\", \
FormFactorizationMethod -> \"Spectral\", DiagonalizationMethod -> \
\"NumericalReconstruction\" or \"Numerical\", GeneratorEquations with \
UnitaryTDiagonal, and irreps without a native variant. UnitarizationMethod -> \
\"BSGSAverage\" is refused there (InapplicableOption).", "Notes"], 
  Cell["TPhaseOrder, PhaseConvention and an explicit DiagonalizationMethod \
apply to Basis -> \"UnitaryTDiagonal\" only; with Basis -> \"Unitary\" they \
are refused (InapplicableOption).", "Notes"], 
  Cell["An explicit FormFactorizationMethod (\"Cholesky\" or \"LDL\") \
unitarizes the active variant on the Wolfram route (the GAP route unitarizes \
GAP's own witness variant). With Basis -> \"UnitaryTDiagonal\", an explicit \
DiagonalizationMethod -> \"Exact\" also takes the Wolfram route, whose \
eigenbasis choice it names.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Options (shared configured settings can override these defaults):", 
   "Notes"], Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["GroupModel"], "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic, \"Original\", \"Permutation\" or \
\"PC\" for new method calculations; PC requires a solvable group. Restoration \
and compatible cache hits do not convert models. Import uses it only when \
computing a new character-validation source.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["StoreGAPState"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["True", "TableText"], Cell["True retains verified \
state across calls; False keeps only call-local temporary checkpoints. Cached \
mathematical values remain available.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["AttemptTimeLimit"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["600", "TableText"], Cell["Positive seconds or \
Infinity, per attempt including verification and saving. Automatic method \
attempts each receive this limit.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["CoreBudget"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Positive integer at most \
$ProcessorCount, or Automatic to use the available count. Sequential \
algorithms run as separate worker processes.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["MemoryBudget"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Positive integer bytes, or \
Automatic using half system memory less current kernel usage. Admission \
estimates and sampled total worker RSS enforce the allocation.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["ProgressFunction"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Automatic shows a notebook \
monitor when a front end is available; None is silent; a Function or user \
symbol receives progress associations. Callbacks should return promptly; \
failures/cancellation clean owned workers.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["FieldMethod"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Automatic, \"Cyclotomic\", \
\"PrimitiveElement\", \"Radical\", \"RootReduce\" or a duplicate-free list of \
these.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Route"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic, \"GAP\" or \"Wolfram\".", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["WorkingPrecision"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["50", "TableText"], 
       Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Tolerance"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["See the method choices in this page's details.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["WitnessVariant"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic, \"SmallestConductor\" or \"Active\".", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Basis"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["\"Unitary\"", "TableText"], Cell["\"Unitary\" requires unitary \
matrices on every recorded generator; \"General\" accepts any verified basis. \
\"UnitaryTDiagonal\" (ComputeGroupRepresentations, the builders and \
TransformGroupRepresentations) additionally requires the assigned T to be \
diagonal, with its phases in the TPhaseOrder order and the PhaseConvention \
applied (the group needs a modular S,T assignment). SetGroupRepresentation \
and ChangeGroupRepBasis accept \"Unitary\" and \"General\"; \
TransformGroupRepresentations \"Unitary\" and \"UnitaryTDiagonal\". For \
DiagonalizeRepresentationT, \"Unitary\" requires unitary input and keeps the \
result unitary.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["UnitarizationMethod"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["\"GroupAverage\" averages \
M^\[Dagger].M over the image of the group; \"GeneratorEquations\" solves \
M^\[Dagger].H.M == H on the generators and chooses a positive solution; \
\"BSGSAverage\" is a native GAP route (automatic representation computation \
and TransformGroupRepresentations in GAP) and is refused where the work runs \
in Wolfram.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["FormFactorizationMethod"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Each method returns B with H == \
B^\[Dagger].B and is verified: \"Cholesky\" the upper-triangular factor, \
\"LDL\" Sqrt[D].L^\[Dagger] from H == L.D.L^\[Dagger], \"Spectral\" the \
positive square root.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["DiagonalizationMethod"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["\"Exact\" and \
\"NumericalReconstruction\" prove every identity exactly and require \
Arithmetic -> \"Exact\"; \"Numerical\" requires Arithmetic -> \"Numerical\"."\
, "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["TPhaseOrder"], 
        "TableText"], Cell["\"Ascending\"", "TableText"], 
       Cell["\"Ascending\" orders the diagonal T by phase in [0,1) \
(nondecreasing); \"Unchanged\" orders basis vectors by their first nonzero \
coordinate, so an already diagonal T keeps its basis. Vectors of one \
eigenvalue keep their order. With ComputeGroupRepresentations, an irrep whose \
diagonal T is in another order (for example from SL2Reps) is diagonalized \
again in GAP.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["PhaseConvention"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["None", "TableText"], Cell["\"FirstSRow\" applies a diagonal \
unitary rephasing after diagonalization: the first basis phase is one, and \
each nonzero first-row entry of S after the first becomes real and \
nonnegative; zero entries keep their phase and S11 is unchanged.", 
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], 
       Cell[BoxData["Arithmetic"], "TableText"], Cell["\"Exact\"", 
        "TableText"], Cell["\"Exact\" proves identities exactly and refuses \
numerical input; \"Numerical\" works at WorkingPrecision (default 50) and \
checks residuals against Tolerance (default 10^(-Floor[p/2])). Tolerance is \
accepted only with numerical arithmetic.", "TableText"]}, 
      {Cell[" ", "TableRowIcon"], Cell[BoxData["Verification"], "TableText"], 
       Cell["Automatic", "TableText"], Cell["Automatic, \"Exact\", \
\"Numerical\" or None (the Validate functions: Automatic, \"Exact\" or \
\"Numerical\"; the modular-form functions have no \"Exact\" route).", 
        "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, 
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.02], Scaled[0.3], 
         Scaled[0.18], Scaled[0.5]}}]], "3ColumnTableMod"], 
  Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["UnitarizeRepresentation", 
      BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> {"UnitarizeRepresentation.nb", 
        None}], "  |  ", ButtonBox["DiagonalizeRepresentationT", 
      BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> 
       {"DiagonalizeRepresentationT.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["ComputeGroupRepresentations", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"ComputeGroupRepresentations.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["AssignModularGenerators", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"AssignModularGenerators.nb", None}]}], "SeeAlso"], 
  Cell["Examples Initialization", "ExamplesInitializationSection"], 
  Cell["Open this notebook in its repository location. GAP must be installed; \
LINS is required for its bounded search page. Evaluate the setup before the \
examples.", "ExampleText"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"Get", "[", RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Nest", "[", RowBox[{"DirectoryName", 
                  ",", RowBox[{"NotebookFileName", "[", "]"}], ",", "5"}], 
                "]"}], ",", "\"Kernel\"", ",", "\"init.m\""}], "}"}], "]"}], 
        "]"}], ";"}]], "ExampleInitialization"], 
  Cell["Basic Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"g", "=", RowBox[{"BuildGroup", 
                "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"GroupPresentation", "[", RowBox[
                     {RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"s\"", ",", "\"t\""}], "}"}], 
                      ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"s^2\"", ",", "\"t^2\"", 
                          ",", "\"(s.t)^3\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{"StoreGAPState", "\[Rule]", "False"}]}], "]"}]}], 
            ",", "id"}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[
         {RowBox[{"id", "=", RowBox[{"Last", "[", RowBox[{"g", "[", 
                "\"IrrepOrder\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
          RowBox[{"SetGroupRepresentation", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", "id", ",", 
              RowBox[{"ChangeRepBasis", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[
                   {"GroupRepresentation", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", "id"}], 
                    "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[
                         {"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[
                         {"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"Basis", "\[Rule]", "\"General\""}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"StoreGAPState", "\[Rule]", "False"}]}], "]"}], ";", 
          RowBox[{"TransformGroupRepresentations", "[", 
            RowBox[{"g", ",", RowBox[{"StoreGAPState", "\[Rule]", 
                "False"}]}], "]"}], ";", RowBox[{"UnitaryRepresentationQ", 
            "[", RowBox[{"GroupRepresentation", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", 
                "id"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input", 
   CellTags -> "VerifiedExample"], Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output"], 
  Cell["Possible Issues", "ExampleSection"], Cell["Invalid input returns a \
structured Failure. Check FailureQ before using the result.", "ExampleText"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"g", "=", RowBox[{"BuildGroup", "[", 
              RowBox[{RowBox[{"GroupPresentation", "[", RowBox[
                   {RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"s\"", ",", "\"t\""}], "}"}], ",", 
                    RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"s^2\"", ",", "\"t^2\"", ",", 
                        "\"(s.t)^3\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", RowBox[
                 {"StoreGAPState", "\[Rule]", "False"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
        ",", RowBox[{"FailureQ", "[", RowBox[
           {"TransformGroupRepresentations", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", 
              RowBox[{"Basis", "\[Rule]", "\"UnitaryTDiagonal\""}]}], "]"}], 
          "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input", CellTags -> "VerifiedErrorExample"], 
  Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output"], Cell["Related Guides", 
   "MoreAboutSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["Constructing finite groups", 
      BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> 
       {"../../Tutorials/ConstructingFiniteGroups.nb", None}]}], 
   "MoreAbout"], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Metadata", "MetadataSection"], 
     Cell["Symbol", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Entity Type"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Paclet Name"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool`", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Context"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool/ref/TransformGroupRepresentations", "Categorization", 
      CellLabel -> "URI"]}, Closed]]}, 
 WindowTitle -> "TransformGroupRepresentations \[LongDash] VVMFTool", 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 850}, TaggingRules -> <|"Paclet" -> "VVMFTool", 
